Great, come on.

291
00:21:47,280 --> 00:21:47,880
Cheers.

292
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:49,320
Cheers.

293
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:50,200
Drink up, drink up.

294
00:21:50,280 --> 00:21:50,800
All right.

295
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:57,240
Cheers.

296
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:57,800
All right.

297
00:22:02,360 --> 00:22:03,120
Come, Shiqi.

298
00:22:03,160 --> 00:22:04,080
Let's have a drink.

299
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,200
It was all a misunderstanding before.

300
00:22:17,680 --> 00:22:18,360
Shiqi.

301
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:37,400
Shiqi

302
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:42,280
I've really spoiled her.

303
00:22:42,360 --> 00:22:43,040
It's fine, it's fine.

304
00:22:43,040 --> 00:22:43,960
Come on, Director Wang.

305
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:45,200
Come, come, come.

306
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:46,200
Come on, let's drink.

307
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:47,280
Let's keep drinking.

308
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,360
Uncle Fan.

309
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:58,240
Director Wang.

310
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:01,320
About what we agreed on tonight...

311
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:03,800
...when you sober up tomorrow morning...

312
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,200
...you can't go back on your word.

313
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:13,880
A gentleman's word is his bond.

314
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:15,120
Good, good, good.

315
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:17,120
Good.

316
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:18,520
I sincerely hope...

317
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:19,960
...that we...

318
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:22,560
...can unite our families.

319
00:23:23,560 --> 00:23:25,120
No need to see me out.

320
00:23:25,120 --> 00:23:26,000
Okay.

321
00:23:26,200 --> 00:23:27,520
Take care, Director Wang.

322
00:23:27,680 --> 00:23:28,600
See you another day.

323
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:29,360
Goodbye.

324
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:30,520
Take care, take care.

325
00:23:37,240 --> 00:23:38,000
Lao Fan.

326
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:44,080
Look at you.

327
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,440
During dinner just now...

328
00:23:45,480 --> 00:23:46,560
...what was with that look on your face?

329
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:47,200
Dad.

330
00:23:50,040 --> 00:23:51,080
Is my marriage...

331
00:23:51,080 --> 00:23:53,720
...just a bargaining chip for your business?

332
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:55,040
I'm your father.

333
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:56,640
Do you think I'd ever hurt you?

334
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:58,320
Everything I'm doing now...

335
00:23:58,320 --> 00:23:59,760
...is all for your own good.

336
00:24:00,160 --> 00:24:01,200
Since I was little...

337
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:06,280
...my mom decided what I wore.

338
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:07,520
What school I went to...

339
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:08,600
...what major I chose...

340
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:09,600
...what kind of life I lived...

341
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:10,480
...and what job I got...

342
00:24:10,480 --> 00:24:11,920
...you arranged absolutely everything.

343
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:15,480
But when it comes to marriage...

344
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:18,120
...this time...

345
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:21,600
...can you please let me choose for myself?

346
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,080
Living in this world...

347
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:24,680
...is all about equivalent exchange.

348
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:26,840
What you want isn't important.

349
00:24:27,080 --> 00:24:29,560
What matters is what you can offer them.

350
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:31,080
But I'm your daughter.

351
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,320
I'm not some commodity for you to trade.

352
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:37,560
You're determined to marry that Vulture...

353
00:24:37,560 --> 00:24:39,120
...and let him take over my company?

354
00:24:40,680 --> 00:24:42,680
Don't think I can't see what you're up to.

355
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:45,280
Throwing yourself at him...

356
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:47,080
...have you no shame?

357
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,080
You had someone watch me?

358
00:24:49,080 --> 00:24:51,600
What else? Was I supposed to just watch you...

359
00:24:51,600 --> 00:24:53,240
...be with that punk?

360
00:24:53,240 --> 00:24:55,120
He might not even be interested in you.

361
00:24:55,120 --> 00:24:55,800
Enough!

362
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:00,440
And about this contract...

363
00:25:00,760 --> 00:25:03,080
When you get engaged to Xiao Wang...

364
00:25:03,360 --> 00:25:05,120
...only then will I sign this contract.

365
00:25:06,440 --> 00:25:07,560
Whether you agree to this contract...

366
00:25:07,560 --> 00:25:08,880
...what does it have to do with them?

367
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,080
I am a businessman.

368
00:25:10,280 --> 00:25:11,920
You should understand this principle.

369
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:14,840
You're getting completely out of line.

370
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:48,960
Granny.

371
00:25:49,280 --> 00:25:50,240
You're awake.

372
00:25:51,440 --> 00:25:52,200
Xiwa.

373
00:25:52,720 --> 00:25:53,400
Granny.

374
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:54,200
You can't take that off.

375
00:25:54,200 --> 00:25:55,920
I brought you some food.

376
00:25:56,240 --> 00:25:57,120
Granny's awake.

377
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:58,840
Granny.

378
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:00,560
I'll go get the doctor.

379
00:26:03,760 --> 00:26:05,000
Granny, you can't touch that.

380
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:08,880
Granny, how are you feeling now?

381
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:10,360
You've been asleep for days.

382
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:13,960
Who... are you?

383
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:16,120
It's me, Xizi.

384
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,840
The Xizi who loves brown sugar glutinous rice cakes.

385
00:26:33,720 --> 00:26:35,320
Xiwa

386
00:26:51,480 --> 00:26:53,800
Late-stage Alzheimer's disease is agony.

387
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:55,520
Aside from memory loss,

388
00:26:55,520 --> 00:26:57,840
physical decline is the most fatal part.

389
00:26:57,880 --> 00:26:58,680
Regardless,

390
00:26:58,680 --> 00:27:01,480
it slowly drains all memory and vitality.

391
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:06,520
Then... is there any chance she can recover?

392
00:27:08,240 --> 00:27:10,120
Talk to her more about the past.

393
00:27:10,120 --> 00:27:11,480
Don't put too much pressure on her.

394
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:13,880
Eventually, getting dressed, eating,

395
00:27:13,880 --> 00:27:16,200
washing up, and using the toilet need help.

396
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:18,480
Her mood will fluctuate.

397
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:20,560
You need to show more care and patience.

398
00:27:21,120 --> 00:27:22,240
At this stage,

399
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:24,080
returning to a familiar environment

400
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,080
would be better for her.

401
00:27:25,960 --> 00:27:26,720
Okay.

402
00:27:26,720 --> 00:27:27,320
Let's go.

403
00:27:27,320 --> 00:27:28,160
Thank you, doctor.

404
00:28:12,120 --> 00:28:12,880
Hello?

405
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:15,840
Ma'am?

406
00:28:17,440 --> 00:28:18,920
Who are you looking for?

407
00:28:22,240 --> 00:28:23,240
Ma'am.

408
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:25,520
Say something.

409
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:27,200
You...

410
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:28,320
Ma'am.

411
00:28:28,640 --> 00:28:30,280
Don't scare me.

412
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:49,480
Ma'am

413
00:29:18,720 --> 00:29:22,400
Why can't I remember?

414
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:39,200
Xiwa.

415
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:42,040
Pour Grandma some water.

416
00:29:42,840 --> 00:29:43,640
All washed.

417
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:46,160
Dry off.

418
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:47,920
Okay.

419
00:29:48,600 --> 00:29:49,400
I poured it.

420
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:29,280
Xiwa

421
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:30,560
Grandma

422
00:30:31,960 --> 00:30:33,160
What's wrong, Grandma?

423
00:30:49,520 --> 00:30:51,120
In here

424
00:30:52,080 --> 00:30:53,920
is the money I saved,

425
00:30:55,200 --> 00:30:56,160
and

426
00:30:56,840 --> 00:30:58,200
your dad

427
00:30:58,840 --> 00:30:59,800
and mom's

428
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:02,360
accident

429
00:31:03,160 --> 00:31:04,600
Compensation.

430
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:08,880
Now that you're back,

431
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:10,840
while I still remember,

432
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:13,320
I'm giving all this

433
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:16,720
to you early.

434
00:31:17,520 --> 00:31:19,520
Grandma, keep it for now.

435
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:20,800
You'll live a long life.

436
00:31:24,640 --> 00:31:27,920
I know my own body.

437
00:31:28,080 --> 00:31:29,960
I've just been holding on,

438
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:34,360
just waiting for you to come back.

439
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:37,760
Now that you're back,

440
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:41,160
keep it safe.

441
00:31:43,960 --> 00:31:44,800
Grandma...

442
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:48,080
You're my grandchild,

443
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:50,360
it should go to you.

444
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,000
If you don't take it, who will?

445
00:31:54,800 --> 00:31:55,840
Keep it safe.

446
00:32:09,720 --> 00:32:11,160
The ancients believed wood

447
00:32:11,160 --> 00:32:13,000
represents immortality,

448
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:16,240
so making a coffin out of wood

449
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:20,440
reflects their wish for eternal life.

450
00:32:22,440 --> 00:32:24,000
Have you ever heard the saying,

451
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:27,440
"Seeing is believing"?

452
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:30,360
But seeing pales to firsthand experience.

453
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:34,800
You want to test the coffin?

454
00:32:35,360 --> 00:32:38,160
When in Shanghai, people I knew tried it.

455
00:32:38,400 --> 00:32:40,080
It made me really want to try it myself.

456
00:32:40,240 --> 00:32:41,440
And now here's my chance.

457
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:43,320
Take off your shoes.

458
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:06,480
How does it feel?

459
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,000
It's amazing.

460
00:33:10,800 --> 00:33:13,040
I felt so peaceful the moment I lay in it.

461
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,840
Lying in this big wooden box,

462
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,840
looking at the world from this angle,

463
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:20,480
it feels completely different.

464
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:21,480
Of course it does.

465
00:33:22,320 --> 00:33:24,040
It feels like, aside from life and death,

466
00:33:24,040 --> 00:33:25,400
everything else is just a scratch.

467
00:33:31,680 --> 00:33:32,720
Wanna try it?

468
00:33:36,160 --> 00:33:37,240
Speaking of firsthand experience,

469
00:33:37,240 --> 00:33:39,560
I've actually played many corpses before.

470
00:34:13,000 --> 00:34:14,240
Cut!

471
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:15,920
Great job, guys!

472
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:16,640
We got it.

473
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:18,720
Great job, guys!

474
00:34:18,720 --> 00:34:20,200
We got it! The director said we got it!

475
00:34:20,200 --> 00:34:20,640
You guys did great.

476
00:34:20,640 --> 00:34:21,560
Stop playing dead.

477
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:22,280
We got it! We got it!

478
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:23,400
Not bad.

479
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:24,840
I heard the director talking about you.

480
00:34:25,240 --> 00:34:27,000
He said your performance... as this corpse...

481
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,240
was incredibly lifelike.

482
00:34:28,240 --> 00:34:28,680
Really?

483
00:34:28,680 --> 00:34:30,080
Even I bought it. Damn right.

484
00:34:30,080 --> 00:34:30,800
Seriously.

485
00:34:31,600 --> 00:34:32,400
Thank you, Director!

486
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,200
Thank you, Director!

487
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:34,840
A lifelike corpse?

488
00:34:35,200 --> 00:34:36,800
Is he complimenting you or insulting you?

489
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:38,760
No matter how well you play a corpse,

490
00:34:38,800 --> 00:34:41,080
you're still nothing but a lousy extra.

491
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:44,280
Give it a try.

492
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:48,120
It definitely feels different.

493
00:34:49,520 --> 00:34:50,120
Okay.

494
00:35:07,560 --> 00:35:08,400
How does it feel?

495
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:17,040
Lying in the real deal feels different.

496
00:35:24,920 --> 00:35:27,000
Daxi, I really can't take this anymore.

497
00:35:27,160 --> 00:35:28,400
You don't look so good today.

498
00:35:28,560 --> 00:35:29,760
Don't go to your part-time job.

499
00:35:29,760 --> 00:35:31,160
Go home and get some rest.

500
00:35:31,480 --> 00:35:32,280
I can't do that.

501
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:33,320
But for today,

502
00:35:33,760 --> 00:35:34,920
you play the toad.

503
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:35,840
I'll play the clown.

504
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:36,600
Why?

505
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:38,760
The last time you used that greasepaint,

506
00:35:38,760 --> 00:35:40,800
you had a severe allergic reaction to it.

507
00:35:48,240 --> 00:35:49,120
Chen Baixi!

508
00:35:51,160 --> 00:35:52,200
What's wrong with you?

509
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:53,120
Are you okay?

510
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:54,680
Slow down, slow down.

511
00:35:54,680 --> 00:35:55,680
Are you okay?

512
00:35:57,640 --> 00:35:58,720
Let me catch my breath.

513
00:35:58,720 --> 00:35:59,040
No...

514
00:35:59,760 --> 00:36:00,400
My shoes!

515
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:03,680
Chen Baixi!

516
00:36:10,120 --> 00:36:11,320
What's going on?

517
00:36:11,680 --> 00:36:13,080
You were lying there perfectly fine.

518
00:36:13,400 --> 00:36:14,120
Are you possessed or something?

519
00:36:14,120 --> 00:36:15,080
You didn't even grab your shoes!

520
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:19,760
It's fine.

521
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:21,960
If you don't want to talk about it, don't.

522
00:36:31,960 --> 00:36:32,720
Actually...

523
00:36:32,720 --> 00:36:36,240
I didn't return because I was blacklisted.

524
00:36:36,440 --> 00:36:37,760
I knew it!

525
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:39,320
What rich lady has that much power?

526
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:44,200
It was because my best friend passed away.

527
00:36:48,680 --> 00:36:50,080
He was my college classmate.

528
00:36:51,480 --> 00:36:53,360
After we graduated,

529
00:36:53,360 --> 00:36:56,320
we worked part-time and acted.

530
00:36:58,120 --> 00:37:00,360
We lived together in a tiny rented room,

531
00:37:01,320 --> 00:37:02,320
ate instant noodles,

532
00:37:02,400 --> 00:37:03,480
and dreamed of becoming actors.

533
00:37:04,840 --> 00:37:05,960
The day he died,

534
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:09,160
he was just cast for a role the next day.

535
00:37:10,280 --> 00:37:11,360
He was so excited.

536
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:14,520
He finally got to show his talent.

537
00:37:14,520 --> 00:37:15,920
Since his graduation,

538
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:17,240
that was his happiest day.

539
00:37:20,200 --> 00:37:21,400
But I never expected...

540
00:37:22,400 --> 00:37:23,200
that night,

541
00:37:24,840 --> 00:37:26,120
he wouldn't make it to dawn.

542
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:29,360
The doctor said it was sudden death.

543
00:37:29,680 --> 00:37:30,880
There was no time to save him.

544
00:37:32,760 --> 00:37:34,520
But I still can't help but wonder,

545
00:37:35,040 --> 00:37:36,360
if that day...

546
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,720
if I hadn't let him go to work that night,

547
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:40,760
or if I had done something more,

548
00:37:40,760 --> 00:37:41,560
would he not have died?

549
00:37:41,560 --> 00:37:42,200
Chen Baixi,

550
00:37:42,520 --> 00:37:43,840
it wasn't your fault.

551
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:48,760
We always think that

552
00:37:49,720 --> 00:37:52,040
if we had done a little more back then,

553
00:37:52,640 --> 00:37:53,880
a little less,

554
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:56,880
or not done something at all,

555
00:37:58,240 --> 00:37:59,840
could we have changed the future?

556
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:03,160
Could we make everything around us better?

557
00:38:04,520 --> 00:38:05,880
But it doesn't work that way.

558
00:38:06,600 --> 00:38:08,840
Some things are simply unpredictable.

559
00:38:10,320 --> 00:38:11,840
birth, aging, sickness, and death...

560
00:38:11,840 --> 00:38:13,120
Joy, sorrow, meeting, and parting...

561
00:38:14,880 --> 00:38:16,360
Life is always full of regrets.

562
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:17,720
I know all that.

563
00:38:19,040 --> 00:38:22,160
But I still think of how excited he was.

564
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:23,920
So I ran away.

565
00:38:27,960 --> 00:38:28,920
Only by putting on a mask

566
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,240
can I hide myself away.

567
00:38:31,720 --> 00:38:32,960
I really don't understand.

568
00:38:33,480 --> 00:38:34,840
Since God gave him hope,

569
00:38:34,840 --> 00:38:36,280
why did He have to take him away?

570
00:38:43,440 --> 00:38:46,040
Well, look at it from another angle.

571
00:38:48,120 --> 00:38:51,920
He was happy when he passed.

572
00:38:51,920 --> 00:38:53,320
Because he left with hope,

573
00:38:54,120 --> 00:38:55,360
instead of regret.

574
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:01,800
We always say tomorrow will be better,

575
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:06,200
but often, we just die tonight.

576
00:39:09,280 --> 00:39:09,880
Why?

577
00:39:18,120 --> 00:39:18,880
Hello, Director Ma.

578
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:19,720
Baixi,

579
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:20,960
the old lady is fading fast!

580
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:22,520
She's holding on to her last breath!

581
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:23,600
Hurry to the hospital!

582
00:39:24,400 --> 00:39:25,280
Granny Xiufang!

583
00:39:27,960 --> 00:39:28,560
Wait for me!

584
00:39:41,320 --> 00:39:42,960
Xiwa!

585
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:52,440
Quick, over here!

586
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:57,200
Granny.

587
00:39:58,120 --> 00:39:59,880
Granny, it's Xizi.

588
00:40:03,760 --> 00:40:04,480
Granny.

589
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:06,160
My child...

590
00:40:06,360 --> 00:40:08,280
Granny has something

591
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,840
to tell you.

592
00:40:12,880 --> 00:40:13,600
Tell me, Granny.

593
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:15,520
My child...

594
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:26,680
Don't look back.

595
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:34,960
Granny!

596
00:40:38,960 --> 00:40:39,920
Granny!

597
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,040
My child...

598
00:42:26,760 --> 00:42:28,640
For twenty years...

599
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:30,120
at home,

600
00:42:30,120 --> 00:42:32,320
I've been eating all alone.

601
00:42:45,160 --> 00:42:47,160
Grandma made this chicken soup

602
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:48,400
for you.

603
00:42:52,040 --> 00:42:53,120
Is it good?

604
00:42:58,160 --> 00:42:59,280
Then,

605
00:42:59,280 --> 00:43:01,800
Grandma will make more for you tomorrow.
